[Music]  i'm emily allred curator at the world  chess hall of fame  in august 2021 people around missouri  commemorated the state's bicentennial as  part of these celebrations a life-size  granite chessboard will be installed at  a new park on adrian's island in  jefferson city missouri  surrounding the board will be 32 images  representing the contributions that  missourians have made in varied fields  including agriculture  music  literature  and sports  the board will also educate visitors  about significant historical moments and  personalities from the state's history  including president harry s truman dredd  and harriet scott's courageous efforts  to gain their freedom innovations of  george washington carver  the project was spearheaded by dr  jeannie karen sinkfield the co-founder  of the st louis chess campus  the chessboard is the eagle scout  project for andrew dowden a live scout  and student at helios catholic high  school in jefferson city missouri  he completed the engravings on the  stones surrounding the chessboard using  an epilogue laser at the scouts bsa  invention campus  around the board will be benches made  from 200 year old wood by life scout  maya thomas a student at kirksville high  school in kirksville missouri as a part  of her eagle scout project  on august 9th the efforts of both scouts  were honored during a ceremony  commemorating the dedication of the  bicentennial bridge which was attended  by governor mike parson lieutenant  governor mike kehoe and the mayor of  jefferson city carrie turjan  a free brochure is available on-site at  the world chess hall of fame  and for download at world chess  worldchesthof.org  it contains passages about the  historical moments memorialized on each  of the squares as well as information  about the efforts of the scouts who made  this project a reality  you

